{"case_id":"T8002","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["attack surface","input semantics","state"],"commit_induced":"YES","maintenance_needed":true,"confidence":97,"affected_functions":["setup_decode_folder","init_decompression","decompress","Bcj2_Decode","seek_pack","extract_pack_stream","archive_read_format_7zip_cleanup"],"reason":"S1 adds materially new 7-Zip BCJ2 decoding behavior that H0 does not adequately exercise. In S0, setup_decode_folder explicitly rejected _7Z_X86_BCJ2; in S1 it accepts two structured four-source forms, loads three sub-streams, initializes BCJ2 state, and invokes the new Bcj2_Decode path. H0 reaches the general 7-Zip reader through archive_read_support_format_all and archive_read_data_block, but only mutates less than 1% of fixed archive images and has no identified BCJ2 seed or control over the required coder and multi-stream relationships. Therefore it cannot reliably reach the newly accepted deep BCJ2 state machine with valid structure.","evidence":["S0 setup_decode_folder returned ARCHIVE_FATAL with \"currently not supported\" whenever folder->coders[i].codec was _7Z_X86_BCJ2.","S1 setup_decode_folder recognizes _7Z_X86_BCJ2 and requires specific relationships including folder->numCoders, numPackedStreams, numInStreams, numOutStreams, and unPackSize.","S1 adds sub_stream_buff, sub_stream_bytes_remaining, tmp_stream_buff, bcj2_p, bcj2_range, bcj2_code, and bcj2_outPos to struct _7zip, establishing new persistent decoder state.","S1 decompress routes codec2 == _7Z_X86_BCJ2 through Bcj2_Decode, whose behavior depends on four coordinated streams and retained bcj_state and odd_bcj_size state.","H0's files list includes 7-Zip fixtures such as test_read_format_7zip_bcj_lzma1.7z, but no fixture identifier denotes BCJ2.","H0 mutates bytes in existing images via image[rand() % size] = (char)rand(), providing no semantic control to create the BCJ2 coder graph and four-pack-stream forms accepted by setup_decode_folder."],"recommended_action":"Add a valid BCJ2 7-Zip fixture covering one or both accepted stream forms and drive it through archive_read_open_memory, archive_read_next_header, and archive_read_data_block; fuzz BCJ2 stream contents and structural size/index fields while preserving enough of the coder graph to reach Bcj2_Decode."}
